@startuml
title An accepted proposal or goal is saved now and applied at period close
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam maxMessageSize 170
participant "Budget graph" as Graph
database "App DB" as DB
database "Budget checkpoint DB" as CP
actor User
participant "Decision service + API" as Decisions
participant "Period-close service" as Close
Graph -> DB : Store pending_user alert\n+ linked advice + proposed cents
Graph -> CP : interrupt(waiting_for alert IDs)
Graph -> DB : Run status = awaiting_user
User -> Decisions : Accept or dismiss alert
Decisions -> DB : Check ownership + pending status
Decisions -> DB : Commit alert.status\n+ advice_log.outcome
note over DB, CP
Decision and checkpoint are separate writes.
The saved decision must survive a failed resume.
end note
Decisions -> CP : Read waiting IDs
Decisions -> Graph : resume_budget_run(alert_id, decision)
alt Other proposals remain
  Graph -> CP : interrupt again
else All proposals decided
  Graph -> DB : persist_state -> ok\nrecord decisions
end
note over Graph, Decisions
Acceptance does not change today's limit.
Graph resume records completion;
the decision service saves alert status.
end note
== Goals: the same shape, per goal (TPC-25) ==
Graph -> DB : Store proposed goals (start_date = next month)\nafter forget_facts clears debts from the state
Graph -> CP : interrupt(waiting_for goal IDs)
User -> Decisions : Accept, dismiss, or stop a goal
Decisions -> DB : Conditional update: proposed -> accepted\n(409 if decided, dated wrongly, or the kind is taken)
Decisions -> Graph : Resume only if the run is paused
note over Decisions, Close
An undecided proposal expires at the close that opens its start month.
A goal's line starts at that close and ends the month of its target date.
end note
== At period end ==
Close -> DB : Load final actuals + accepted proposals\n+ accepted goals; expire undecided proposals
Close -> DB : Add one line per accepted goal (group goal)\nin the next period
Close -> Close : Existing pure close_period function:\naccepted number wins; otherwise fixed actual\nor 70% old + 30% actual, clamped +/-15%
Close -> DB : Atomic close old period\n+ create next period and lines
note over Decisions, Close
Late decisions get a 409; a failed resume
is finished from the rows.
end note
@enduml
